<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.10.1: The Vertex and Intercepts of a Function</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02498</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.10.1: The Vertex and Intercepts of a Function</md:title>
    <md:uuid>0730bab2-f5b5-4174-8958-f4dc019489b9</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>These expressions each define the same function.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(x^2+6x+8\) </item>
  <item> \((x+2)(x+4)\) </item>
  <item> \((x+3)^2−1\) </item>
</list>
<para>Without graphing or doing any calculations, determine where the following features would be on a graph that represents the function.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="57d2db6d-0cf4-441c-a4e6-5ec5d2a0390b" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6f6efa7e-aa7e-4569-8a0f-891502cd7b1b" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-3">
    <problem>
      <para>The \(x\)-coordinate of the <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">vertex (of a graph)</term>.</para>
      <para>Enter the \(x\)-coordinate.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex is -3.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  
  <!--Q2a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6201a064-001a-4537-9c4a-848ca8f0cc73" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-1">
    <problem>
      <para>The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex (of a graph).</para>
      <para>Enter the \(y\)-coordinate. </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex is -1.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="a9fb89d7-db8d-4dfe-afa4-6c02d453f179" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0"> ----------------------------------------

  <!--Q#-->
  <exercise data-content-id="380ada69-6116-46ec-b904-b6ac6d41ea2f" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\((-2,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((-4,0)\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((-2,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((-6,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((-4,0)\\)&quot;,&quot;\\((-8,0)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para><emphasis>Select both</emphasis> <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">\(x\)-intercepts</term>.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The \(x\)-intercepts are \((-2,0)\) and \((-4,0)\).</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->

  ------------------------------------
